Brief Explanation of Components
Root Directory



BSK_masters.py: Likely contains master configurations or settings for the Basilisk simulation environment

Core Directory

run.py: Main entry point for running the simulation
spacecraft_fault_cli.py: Command-line interface for spacecraft fault simulations
spacecraft_fault_gui.py: GUI version for spacecraft fault simulations
spacecraft_simulator_gui.py: Main GUI for the spacecraft simulator
fault_loader.py: Utility for loading fault scenarios
style.py: Styling configurations for the GUI
gui_tab/: Contains different tabs for the GUI interface

Various tab implementations (constellation, fault, target, etc.) for the simulator interface



Faults Directory

Contains modules for different types of spacecraft faults:

battery_fault.py: Battery-related fault simulations
encoder_fault.py: Encoder-related fault simulations
friction_fault.py: Friction-related fault simulations
powerlimit_fault.py: Power limitation fault simulations
rw_fault.py: Reaction wheel fault simulations



Other Directories

logs/: Likely stores simulation log output
models/: Probably contains spacecraft or component models
plots/: May store generated plots from simulations
plotting/: Contains plotting utilities and functions
scenarios/: Stores predefined simulation scenarios
Vizfile/: Likely contains visualization configuration or output

The project appears to be a spacecraft simulation environment with a focus on fault simulation and analysis, with both GUI and CLI interfaces available.



BskSim/
├── BSK_masters.py              # Master script for Basilisk simulations
├── Readme                      # Main README file
├── core/                       # Core simulator modules
│   ├── fault_loader.py         # Unified interface for fault modules
│   ├── gui_tab/                # GUI tab components
│   │   ├── __init__.py         # Package initialization
│   │   ├── base_tab.py         # Base class for tabs
│   │   ├── constellation_tab.py# Constellation management tab
│   │   ├── fault_tab.py        # Fault configuration tab
│   │   ├── output_tab.py       # Output settings tab
│   │   ├── target_tab.py       # Target management tab
│   │   └── visualization_tab.py# Visualization settings tab
│   ├── run_fault_simulator.py  # Runner script for the GUI
│   ├── rw_fault_help.py        # Help content module
│   ├── spacecraft_simulation.py # Backend simulation engine (needs fixing)
│   ├── spacecraft_simulator_gui.py # Main GUI application
│   └── style.py                # GUI styling module
├── faults/                     # Fault simulation modules
│   ├── battery_fault.py        # Battery fault simulation
│   ├── encoder_fault.py        # Encoder fault simulation
│   ├── friction_fault.py       # Friction fault simulation
│   ├── powerlimit_fault.py     # Power limit fault simulation
│   └── rw_fault.py             # Base reaction wheel fault simulation
├── logs/                       # Simulation log files (created on first run)
├── models/                     # Basilisk model configurations
│   ├── BSK_Dynamics.py         # Spacecraft dynamics models
│   ├── BSK_FormationDynamics.py# Formation flying dynamics models 
│   ├── BSK_FormationFsw.py     # Formation flying flight software models
│   └── BSK_Fsw.py              # Flight software models
├── plots/                      # Simulation plots (created on first run)
├── plotting/                   # Plotting utility files
│   └── BSK_Plotting.py         # Basilisk plotting utilities
├── scenarios/                  # Predefined simulation scenarios
└── Vizfile/                    # Visualization binary files (created on first run)
    └── _VizFiles/              # Directory for Vizard binary files


    Core Capabilities

Constellation Management

Create and configure multiple satellites with custom orbital parameters
Support for various formation configurations
Individual spacecraft property customization


Fault Simulation

Inject four fault types: friction, power limit, encoder, and battery
Configure fault parameters (magnitude, timing, affected wheel)
Support for periodic and one-time faults
Apply faults to specific satellites and their respective plots as well 


Target Management

Define ground locations with name, coordinates, and color
Assign targets to specific satellites
Visualize targets on Earth in simulation


Visualization

Configure camera position and field of view
Single camera view in Vizard for entire constellation
3D visualization of spacecraft, Earth, and targets


Results Analysis

Generate plots of spacecraft behavior and fault effects
Comprehensive simulation summary
Binary file output for Vizard visualization



GUI Structure

Constellation Tab: Configure satellites and orbital parameters
Fault Tab: Set up fault parameters for selected satellites
Targets Tab: Manage ground locations and assignments
Visualization Tab: Configure camera and display settings
Output Tab: Set simulation parameters and logging options
Results Tab: View and analyze simulation output

Vizard Output

3D visualization of all satellites in constellation
Earth model with target markers
Spacecraft components including reaction wheels
Fault effects visible in spacecraft behavior
Time controls for playback and analysis
Camera view from selected spacecraft perspective

Workflow

Configure constellation of satellites
Set up faults on specific spacecraft
Define and assign targets
Configure visualization settings
Run simulation
Analyze results through plots and 3D visualization

The system enables engineers to study fault propagation in spacecraft systems, analyze constellation performance, and develop fault mitigation strategies through an intuitive, interactive interface.


